{{Tabber
|Passives|
{{Skill/Passive
|name     = Soul Counter
|meter    = Soul bar.png
|desc     = The user always had a Soul counter on their screen. Souls could be collected using the Z move on enemies, or by killing someone with any soul move. It could then be used to summon Buddies. The maximum amount of Souls was nine. Following the revamp, the user could collect a maximum of two souls at any given time when using the Z move on multiple NPCs/players.
* Performing the X move will increase the Calm meter.
* Performing the Z and C move will increase the Fury meter. (Not to be confused with the [[Fury Meter]] of some [[Transformation|transformation fruits]])
The Calm and Fury mode were unique features of the Soul Fruit. Soul counter would be shown above the Soul fruit UI that would indicate what mode the user was currently in.
* If the marking on the meter was in the middle, the user would be in Neutral mode which provided no effect.
* If the marking is on the Blue side of the meter, the user would be in Calm Mode. Calm mode increased the AoE of X move.
* If the marking is on the Red side of the meter, the user would be in Fury mode. Fury mode increased the damage of C move.
* If the marking was at the limit of increasing on any mode, the user's V move would get a significant boost in damage.
}}

